WEBVTT

00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:23.840
<i>Every day I keep wondering if</i>
<i>there's something missing.</i>

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:31.190
<i>I still want to keep feeling my</i>
<i>heart beating in anticipation.</i>

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:38.920
<i>Ideals are far out of reach, but</i>
<i>reality is within my grasp.</i>

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:44.990
<i>It's not easy standing against the wind,</i>
<i>but as long as I keep smiling...</i>

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:49.770
<i>... staying true to myself,</i>
<i>I'll become stronger.</i>

00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:57.540
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll find him and take my chance.</i>

00:00:57.610 --> 00:01:04.520
<i>I'll make the whole world stop</i>
<i>to see the angel that I'll be.</i>

00:01:04.590 --> 00:01:12.450
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll meet the man of my dreams.</i>

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:20.120
<i>Nothing can slow me down. Tomorrow</i>
<i>is just around the corner.</i>

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:36.550
The thieves have
likely...

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:39.920
...considered the salability
of the vehicles.

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:43.550
After removing the lock cylinders from
the trunks of the targeted cars...

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:45.950
...they produce new keys
to match the locks.

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:47.960
Then the cars are likely
shipped using...

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:53.020
...a small foreign-registered freighter
for export to overseas markets.

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:04.270
Why are you stopping
me?

00:02:11.350 --> 00:02:16.220
FILE. 51
BOKUTO'S BEST
INVESTIGATION
PARTNERS

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:22.160
"Luxury Auto Theft Task Force"

00:02:28.570 --> 00:02:30.430
Inspector Kinoshita.

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:32.510
Is something on
your mind?

00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:35.500
Sergeant Kobayakawa's
report.

00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:37.300
Oh?

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:43.540
She's written up a profile, their projected
routes, and even the arrest procedures.

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:47.040
I'm amazed she's put so much
thought into this.

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:52.090
There they are!
Natsumi! Miyuki!

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:52.430
See you later!

00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:54.390
Hi!

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:58.020
I read your report,
Miyuki.

00:02:58.130 --> 00:02:58.970
It was fantastic!

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:00.300
Yeah?

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:04.770
Actually, I had somebody help me.
Someone completely unexpected.

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:06.070
Unexpected?

00:03:06.070 --> 00:03:07.800
Yes, that's right.

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:10.940
<i>"Miyuki?"</i>

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:16.550
<i>"Yes. We'll give you what</i>
<i>we know so far."</i>

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:20.680
<i>"Hi. I found out something interesting,</i>
<i>about that used car lot."</i>

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:22.060
<i>"Hi."</i>

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:24.020
"Hello."

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:31.060
That sounds like some
solid information.

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:47.410
Here you are, Detective.

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:49.380
Thanks.

00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:59.610
I wonder if that truck's even
going to move today.

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:07.100
It will. You'll see, it's perfect
for moving stolen cars.

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:12.640
But there was another
theft just yesterday.

00:04:12.740 --> 00:04:16.840
I doubt they'll strike
two days in a row.

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:19.110
That's probably just what they're thinking.

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:20.880
Huh?

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:32.250
Perhaps we should let the people
in Traffic go home on standby.

00:04:32.430 --> 00:04:33.690
Well...

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:35.260
What is it?

00:04:35.260 --> 00:04:38.930
I think tonight's the night.

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:43.570
I feel the same
way, Chief.

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:49.280
All right. We'll send everyone
home to rest up.

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:51.970
Contact all units
immediately.

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:57.950
I'm pooped.

00:04:58.050 --> 00:05:00.350
We didn't get anything
today.

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:03.490
Can't count on getting results
so soon.

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:07.360
What?

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:15.020
I thought that way up until a while ago.
It's what I'd have said to you.

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:19.330
Have I changed?

00:05:19.510 --> 00:05:22.300
I'm going to
go for it.

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:24.970
I don't feel good about myself
the way things are.

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:30.980
Yeah, I'm a little
tired, too.

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:38.310
Miyuki, I'm going
to bed.

00:05:38.430 --> 00:05:40.390
Okay. 'Night.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:24.670
Hey. Wake up.

00:06:24.670 --> 00:06:27.200
Huh? Detective!

00:06:27.370 --> 00:06:28.540
Call the station.

00:06:28.540 --> 00:06:31.510
Yes, sir!

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:37.540
Natsumi.

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:41.540
Command to all units.
State your positions.

00:06:42.190 --> 00:06:46.520
The truck and trailer are moving. Shift
to phase 2. Await further instructions.

00:06:47.990 --> 00:06:50.860
Nikaidou. Contact everyone
at home on standby.

00:06:51.030 --> 00:06:52.620
Yes, sir!

00:06:52.730 --> 00:06:54.700
I've already contacted
everyone.

00:06:55.170 --> 00:06:58.730
Huh? Oh?

00:06:58.910 --> 00:07:03.140
Sergeant Aoi. Update me on the
patrol car arrangements.

00:07:37.780 --> 00:07:40.970
Just past four.

00:07:41.150 --> 00:08:01.600
Detective.

00:08:01.700 --> 00:08:02.900
They're leaving!

00:08:02.900 --> 00:08:04.870
Stay calm.

00:08:08.040 --> 00:08:10.100
Check out the
warehouse.

00:08:10.210 --> 00:08:14.770
If the Benz is not inside, then
it's in the trailer.

00:08:14.950 --> 00:08:16.940
Yes, sir.

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:18.680
Hey!

00:08:19.220 --> 00:08:20.880
Be careful.

00:08:21.050 --> 00:08:23.020
Sir.

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:40.200
Stupid fool.

00:08:42.380 --> 00:08:44.970
Calling all patrol
cars.

00:08:45.350 --> 00:08:47.470
Just in from
Unit 18.

00:08:47.580 --> 00:08:50.780
The trailer with the stolen cars just entered
Route 6 at the Komagata ramp.

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:53.410
It's currently heading
south.

00:08:53.520 --> 00:08:55.680
All units, proceed
to level 3.

00:08:55.790 --> 00:08:58.780
Pursue the truck
when sighted.

00:08:59.630 --> 00:09:01.530
Unit 18, huh?

00:09:02.130 --> 00:09:04.620
Yeah. Way to go, Detective
Tokuno!

00:09:04.800 --> 00:09:07.490
Let's take the Hakozaki Interchange and
the Metropolitan Expressway.

00:09:07.670 --> 00:09:10.300
Okay.

00:09:10.740 --> 00:09:14.730
"Hakozaki"
The suspect has passed the Hakozaki
Interchange and has entered Route 9.

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:22.380
"Route 9 Fukagawa-line"

00:09:45.170 --> 00:09:49.010
Just as Inspector Kinoshita predicted, the
culprits are going to the Bayshore Route.

00:09:51.080 --> 00:09:54.240
Calling all units. Proceed
to Plan A.

00:09:55.250 --> 00:09:59.450
Block all exits along the Metropolitan Express-
way between Hakozaki and Ooi.

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:09.590
Detective Tokuno. Tsujimoto
here! We're in pursuit.

00:10:09.760 --> 00:10:11.700
You're the first ones here!

00:10:11.700 --> 00:10:13.670
You're the first ones here!
Detective!

00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:16.940
You made it, too?

00:10:16.940 --> 00:10:19.000
You made it, too?
Yes!

00:10:19.240 --> 00:10:20.710
There's Nakajima.

00:10:21.540 --> 00:10:24.510
Can't have you forgetting
about the White Hawk.

00:10:24.940 --> 00:10:26.650
Ooh, Kennie!

00:10:26.650 --> 00:10:29.410
Ooh, Kennie!
Don't call him that!

00:10:29.580 --> 00:10:31.550
The gang's
all here.

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:43.390
Gee, this is really getting
nerve-racking.

00:10:43.560 --> 00:10:45.100
I agree.

00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:46.660
Uh-oh.

00:10:46.770 --> 00:10:48.170
Look at that Alfa Romeo.

00:10:48.170 --> 00:10:51.140
I wonder what's wrong with it.

00:10:58.910 --> 00:11:00.640
Oh no, now what are
we going to do?

00:11:00.810 --> 00:11:02.340
We can't just
ignore them.

00:11:02.450 --> 00:11:03.610
Contact Detective
Tokuno.

00:11:03.780 --> 00:11:06.220
Will do.

00:11:10.320 --> 00:11:12.050
Are you all right?

00:11:12.160 --> 00:11:13.590
Hello?

00:11:13.690 --> 00:11:15.160
Are you okay?

00:11:15.260 --> 00:11:16.850
Hello?

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:32.270
Aoi!

00:11:48.830 --> 00:11:51.850
Damn! We're going to
lose that trailer.

00:11:55.670 --> 00:11:57.730
We have to help Detective
Tokuno.

00:11:57.900 --> 00:12:00.900
Let's do it!
Oh, no!

00:12:01.110 --> 00:12:02.580
They must be together.

00:12:02.580 --> 00:12:05.440
You're right.

00:12:08.380 --> 00:12:10.610
Aoi!

00:12:10.780 --> 00:12:13.680
An ambulance is
on the way.

00:12:13.850 --> 00:12:14.450
Who did it?

00:12:14.450 --> 00:12:16.420
A red Alfa Romeo.

00:12:18.560 --> 00:12:22.490
How could he do
that to Aoi?!

00:12:22.600 --> 00:12:26.550
Let's do it, Natsumi. We'll show
them how real brakes work!

00:12:26.870 --> 00:12:28.800
Yeah!

00:12:35.110 --> 00:12:36.440
Here he comes.

00:12:36.440 --> 00:12:38.970
Okay.

00:12:39.150 --> 00:12:41.640
Now!

00:12:42.180 --> 00:12:43.980
Damn!

00:12:45.150 --> 00:12:47.120
Natsumi!

00:13:03.270 --> 00:13:04.300
Are you okay?

00:13:04.300 --> 00:13:06.670
Yes.

00:13:07.870 --> 00:13:09.140
Detective!

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:11.700
Shut up! Or you'll bite your tongue!

00:13:27.890 --> 00:13:30.760
Strange. The trailer's
nowhere in sight.

00:13:30.930 --> 00:13:32.920
No! That
can't be!

00:13:33.100 --> 00:13:35.570
We should have passed
it by now.

00:13:35.740 --> 00:13:37.970
It wouldn't be heading toward
Urayasu, would it?

00:13:38.140 --> 00:13:39.510
Oh, no!

00:13:39.510 --> 00:13:42.200
Got it! We've spotted the trailer!

00:13:42.310 --> 00:13:45.210
We're in pursuit, heading
for Haneda.

00:13:58.220 --> 00:14:00.190
What'd you do
that for?

00:14:02.160 --> 00:14:04.430
Kobayakawa! Where
are you going?

00:14:05.130 --> 00:14:07.400
Hey! Kobayakawa!

00:14:07.400 --> 00:14:09.270
Bokuto Unit 4! Come back, immediately!

00:14:09.370 --> 00:14:11.170
Sergeant Kobayakawa!

00:14:11.170 --> 00:14:15.700
Inspector. Consider the thieves' methods.

00:14:16.240 --> 00:14:19.700
They've always been able to
see through our strategy.

00:14:20.080 --> 00:14:22.640
They're aware of
our movements.

00:14:22.750 --> 00:14:28.020
Considering that, they must know that we
have control of the Bayshore Route.

00:14:28.690 --> 00:14:30.660
You mean
that...

00:14:30.920 --> 00:14:32.790
There they
are!

00:14:32.960 --> 00:14:36.860
There's no guarantee that they'll be using
Tokyo Bay to load their cargo.

00:14:37.030 --> 00:14:41.760
The trailer appears to be exiting at the
Daikoku ramp! Get them there!

00:14:41.930 --> 00:14:43.990
That's not the
same truck.

00:14:44.100 --> 00:14:46.970
They must have switched
at Ariake Junction.

00:14:47.140 --> 00:14:48.740
I agree.

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:50.210
Nakajima!

00:14:50.210 --> 00:14:53.300
We're the only ones on the right trail.

00:14:54.180 --> 00:14:58.240
Command to Bokuto Unit
4. Shift to Plan B.

00:14:58.350 --> 00:15:02.310
Kobayakawa, you do what
you think is best.

00:15:02.820 --> 00:15:04.060
Roger.

00:15:04.060 --> 00:15:06.320
How did you know, Miyuki?

00:15:07.230 --> 00:15:11.060
Because that's what
I would have done.

00:15:17.270 --> 00:15:20.240
You in the trailer!
Pull over!

00:15:24.380 --> 00:15:25.640
Damn!

00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:27.300
Kobayakawa was right!

00:15:27.880 --> 00:15:29.610
They tricked us.

00:15:30.020 --> 00:15:31.540
Contact Headquarters!

00:15:31.650 --> 00:15:34.120
They got us
this time!

00:15:34.250 --> 00:15:34.790
"Luxury Car Theft Task Force"

00:15:34.790 --> 00:15:37.690
Bokuto Unit 4 here!
Come in, command.

00:15:38.220 --> 00:15:40.920
Command here. State
your position.

00:15:41.090 --> 00:15:44.620
We're on Mejiro Street, about to
enter the Kan-etsu Expressway.

00:15:44.930 --> 00:15:47.460
Hmm?

00:15:48.370 --> 00:15:49.890
Inspector Arizuka!

00:15:50.070 --> 00:15:50.800
What's happening?

00:15:50.800 --> 00:15:53.770
The trailer just ran the tollbooth!

00:15:55.310 --> 00:15:57.280
Who's in pursuit?

00:15:57.440 --> 00:16:01.470
Kobayakawa, Tsujimoto and Nakajima,
all from the Traffic Section.

00:16:02.080 --> 00:16:05.020
So the thieves
have...

00:16:05.820 --> 00:16:09.220
The girls have far exceeded
my expectations.

00:16:09.720 --> 00:16:13.160
You don't need to stay here anymore.
Get out there immediately.

00:16:13.330 --> 00:16:15.590
Yes, sir!

00:16:20.670 --> 00:16:22.170
At this rate...

00:16:22.170 --> 00:16:25.100
This way will take them to Niigata port.

00:16:25.270 --> 00:16:27.970
Yoriko here. Come
in Bokuto Unit 4.

00:16:29.040 --> 00:16:31.010
Yoriko! How's
Aoi?

00:16:32.750 --> 00:16:35.340
How is she?!
Tell us!

00:16:35.520 --> 00:16:38.640
They said it's nothing
serious.

00:16:38.820 --> 00:16:41.010
Sorry to worry
you.

00:16:41.190 --> 00:16:42.120
Aoi!

00:16:42.120 --> 00:16:44.020
Aoi!
Yoriko gets so worked up.

00:16:44.190 --> 00:16:47.890
Well, wouldn't you? Miyuki.
Natsumi. Nakajima.

00:16:47.990 --> 00:16:50.960
You've got to stop
that trailer.

00:16:51.500 --> 00:16:53.330
We will, Yoriko!

00:16:53.330 --> 00:16:54.960
We will, Yoriko!
Leave it to us!

00:17:01.040 --> 00:17:03.530
That van!

00:17:03.980 --> 00:17:06.740
Oh, no! Tsujimoto!
Kobayakawa!

00:17:24.630 --> 00:17:26.600
Nakajima!

00:17:39.950 --> 00:17:41.080
Are you okay?

00:17:41.080 --> 00:17:43.840
Nakajima? I... I...

00:17:44.020 --> 00:17:45.750
Are you all right?

00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:49.240
Don't worry. It's just a scrape.

00:17:49.360 --> 00:17:52.560
Kobayakawa. Be careful.

00:17:52.560 --> 00:17:54.790
Nakajima.

00:17:54.960 --> 00:17:57.020
What about me?

00:18:11.310 --> 00:18:14.800
We've got the support of the Saitama
and Gunma Police Forces.

00:18:14.910 --> 00:18:16.640
We're on our way
by helicopter.

00:18:16.750 --> 00:18:19.120
Whatever you do, don't
do anything reckless!

00:18:19.290 --> 00:18:21.750
We're Traffic Police. We've
got to stop that trailer.

00:18:21.850 --> 00:18:26.050
We can't let these reckless drivers get
away with it. Let's do what it takes.

00:18:26.230 --> 00:18:27.630
Wait! That's too dangerous!

00:18:27.630 --> 00:18:29.720
Over and out.

00:18:30.230 --> 00:18:32.200
Wait!

00:18:32.300 --> 00:18:34.990
H... How could
they?

00:18:35.170 --> 00:18:37.530
You can't stop
those two.

00:18:38.270 --> 00:18:41.730
They're going to do their
own thing now.

00:18:41.840 --> 00:18:46.340
The only thing we can do is
take full responsibility.

00:18:46.450 --> 00:18:49.510
That's it.

00:18:49.680 --> 00:18:52.340
We have to give young
people a chance.

00:18:52.450 --> 00:18:56.350
They're the ones who can change the
world if they put their minds to it.

00:18:56.460 --> 00:18:58.690
It's always been
that way.

00:19:12.410 --> 00:19:14.370
Look, Miyuki!

00:19:18.680 --> 00:19:21.480
Maybe we shouldn't have been pretending
to be the tough guys.

00:19:21.650 --> 00:19:23.410
They've lost all
their buddies.

00:19:23.920 --> 00:19:26.250
They're getting backed
into a corner.

00:19:26.420 --> 00:19:30.550
We can't even begin to guess what
they're going to do next.

00:19:30.720 --> 00:19:32.160
Well?

00:19:32.160 --> 00:19:33.660
Of course.

00:19:33.660 --> 00:19:34.830
Well?
Of course. Nitro...

00:19:34.830 --> 00:19:36.800
Well?
Of course. Nitro... On!

00:19:54.810 --> 00:19:57.870
What the hell kind of
patrol car is that?

00:20:29.380 --> 00:20:30.480
What the?!

00:20:30.480 --> 00:20:32.970
Didn't the Mercedes crush them?

00:20:49.440 --> 00:20:51.600
Damn it!

00:20:56.410 --> 00:20:58.430
35 km per hour over
the speed limit...

00:20:58.610 --> 00:21:00.440
...ignoring designated
traffic signs...

00:21:00.910 --> 00:21:03.880
...failure to heed the
rules of the road...

00:21:04.320 --> 00:21:06.080
...improper use of
driving lanes...

00:21:06.250 --> 00:21:08.550
...improper securing of cargo...

00:21:08.550 --> 00:21:10.420
...and reckless driving...

00:21:10.590 --> 00:21:14.220
...in an improperly loaded
vehicle...

00:21:14.730 --> 00:21:17.700
You're SO Under Arrest!
You're SO Under Arrest!

00:21:33.910 --> 00:21:35.780
We sure did it!

00:21:35.780 --> 00:21:37.750
Yeah.

00:21:39.020 --> 00:21:42.010
Thanks, Natsumi.

00:21:42.120 --> 00:21:44.920
I'm really glad
I met you.

00:21:45.090 --> 00:21:47.890
And me!
Thanks.

00:21:48.890 --> 00:21:52.090
We'll be able to work together
again, right?

00:21:52.200 --> 00:21:54.100
What?

00:21:54.100 --> 00:22:01.060
I was to be reassigned to Bokuto
Traffic Section once this was solved.

00:22:02.010 --> 00:22:03.980
I figured as
much.

00:22:05.180 --> 00:22:07.810
And you were
right.

00:22:08.110 --> 00:22:11.820
Credit translations to follow ending song.
<i>Every time I fall out of love...</i>

00:22:11.820 --> 00:22:13.250
<i>Every time I fall out of love...</i>

00:22:13.250 --> 00:22:14.350
Yoriko, thanks for caring about me.

00:22:14.350 --> 00:22:17.560
<i>... everything that I see turns monochrome.</i>
Yoriko, thanks for caring about me.

00:22:17.560 --> 00:22:24.130
"Serial Auto Case Solved"

00:22:24.130 --> 00:22:24.500
"Bokuto Police Station..."

00:22:24.500 --> 00:22:28.170
We often used to go see the
<i>games at the stadium...</i>

00:22:28.170 --> 00:22:30.840
Way to go! My mentors!

00:22:30.840 --> 00:22:34.540
<i>... but the good old days mean</i>
<i>nothing to me anymore.</i>

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:37.180
<i>Lately, there has been a wave of luxury car</i>
<i>thefts throughout the city.</i>

00:22:37.180 --> 00:22:37.240
<i>... but the good old days mean</i>
<i>nothing to me anymore.</i>

00:22:37.240 --> 00:22:40.380
<i>The thieves tried to make a run forthe</i>
<i>Kan-etsu Expressway...</i>

00:22:40.380 --> 00:22:40.400
You hungry too?
